2. THE UNITED STATES GOVERNMENT RECORDS
----------------------------------------
Draft registration cards, passenger lists, morning and day reports, burial and
removal cards, Graves Registration Service plats, regimental general orders,
service certifications, and the U.S. Army Signal Corps photograph (negative no.
154573) are works of the United States Government or records held by the
National Archives. They are in the PUBLIC DOMAIN and are not covered by the
licence above. Use them freely.

The regimental histories of the 110th Infantry (1920) and the 317th Infantry,
and "Soldiers of the Great War" (1920), are published works whose copyright has
expired.


