redistribute them on the strength of this repository:

  * assets/lengel-note20-gas.jpg
      A page image from Edward G. Lengel, "To Conquer Hell: The Meuse-Argonne,
      1918" (New York: Henry Holt and Co., 2008). Quotations from the same work
      appear throughout and are cited in place.

  * assets/obituary-kokos.jpg
      Obituary, Blairsville Dispatch, 10 July 1958, retrieved via Newspapers.com.

  * assets/headstone-david.jpg, assets/grave-kokos.jpg
      Photographs of grave markers by third-party contributors.

  * assets/jodie-p1.jpg, assets/jodie-p2.jpg
      Written recollection of David H. Bryant by Jodie Sweat, 22 August 2026.
      Copyright in this testimony belongs to its author, who supplied it for
      this account. It is reproduced here by her permission and is NOT covered
      by the licence above. Do not reuse it without asking her.

  * assets/map-terrain-chatel.jpg
      A modern elevation map derived from third-party elevation data. Included
      as illustration of the ground; not a period document and not relicensed.


4. A REQUEST CONCERNING SERGEANT WILLIAM KOKOS
-----------------------------------------------
This is a request, not a licence term, and it is made in earnest.

The pages concerning William Kokos set out the manner of his death in 1958 and
reproduce the coroner's certificate that records it. He never married, left no
descendants, and the last member of his family named in any document was a
brother in 1958. There is nobody left to be consulted, and nobody left to
object. That is a reason for more care, not less.

Please do not repost, republish or circulate the Kokos material outside private
research correspondence. If quoting him serves the history, quote him. If it
does not, please ask first.

